    Question: The seats of a bus are arranged in 23 rows of 4 seats. At the start, 16 people climb. At the first stop, 15 people board the bus and 3 get off. At the second stop, 17 people get on the bus and 10 get off. How many empty seats are there after the second stop? Think step by step. Answer:At the first stop, 15 people board the bus and 3 get off, so there are 15 - 3 = 12 more people on the bus. At the second stop, 17 people get on the bus and 10 get off, so there are 12 + 17 - 10 = 19 more people on the bus. Therefore, after the second stop, there are 23 rows x 4 seats = 92 seats in total. After the second stop, there are 92 - 19 = 73 empty seats. #### 73 The answer is: 73

