    Question: Philip has a farm with animals. He has 20 cows, 50% more ducks. Philip also has as many pigs as one-fifth of ducks and cows in total. How many animals does Philip have on his farm? Think step by step. Answer:Philip has 20 cows. He has 50% more ducks, so he has 50/100 * 20 = 10 ducks. Philip also has as many pigs as one-fifth of ducks and cows in total, so he has 10/5 * (20 + 10) = 10 * 30 = 300 pigs. In total, Philip has 20 cows + 10 ducks + 300 pigs = 330 animals on his farm. #### 330 The answer is: 330

